Use this checklist to find red flags:

Indicator	What to Check
🧑‍✉️ Sender's Address	Is it fake? Example: secure@paypal.com.fake.com

🧠 Spelling Errors	Phishing emails often have grammar/spelling mistakes

🔗 Links in Email	Hover your mouse on them. Do they go to a strange or fake website?

📎 Attachments	Unusual or dangerous file types (like .exe, .zip)

⚠️ Urgent Language	Examples: “Your account will be locked!” or “Click now!”

🔁 Mismatch in Display Name and Email	Sender name says “Google” but email says random@unknown.ru

🧾 Header Info (Advanced)	Use https://mxtoolbox.com/EmailHeaders.aspx to check who really sent the email
